invariant: INV-48
file: src/mlkem_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the rejection step on AVX2 takes the even lanes from the shifted
  pairs and the odd ones from the masked pairs, so each group's d1 and d2
  are each read from the other's bits. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the
  line, so the script builds bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and
  runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    return _mm256_blend_epi16(low, high, 0xaa);
--- new
    return _mm256_blend_epi16(low, high, 0x55);
